fof_version: '0.1'
type: enemy
id: bought_blade
name: Blade of the Bought
ruleset:
  modules:
  - id: base
    version: 0.1.0
enemy:
  tier: mook
  attack_modifier: 1
  armor: light
  techniques: []
  special: null
  description: Contracted muscle in a matched coat — grey wool, cut plainly, the company's
    mark stitched at the shoulder where a house badge would sit. In a city where everyone
    wears a knife to a ball, sixteen people wearing the same coat is the thing that stands
    out.
  disposition: Professional. Not cruel, not enthusiastic, and paying close attention to the
    terms.
  first_target: Whoever the contract names. Everyone else is an obstacle to be moved.
  triggers:
  - Will not pursue past the boundary the contract specifies, and knows exactly where that
    is.
  - Fights to the terms — a contract to detain produces no killing blows, and everyone on
    both sides can tell the difference.
  morale: Down two of four and the rest disengage in order. Nobody in the Bought has ever
    been paid enough to die for a clause.
  organization: Sixteen walked into the trade district at dusk. Four hold the Boranis gatehouse;
    the rest hold the outer perimeter and are not on the scene card.
  notes: 'TR breakdown: offense(+1 → 3) + durability(Mook → 0) + armor(light → 1) + techniques(0)
    = 4.


    MODULE RESKIN (Oraga Night). Flavour fields only — description and organization. Tier,
    resolve, attack_modifier, armor, techniques and special are the Bestiary''s and must stay
    identical to enemies/bought_blade.fof; a test asserts it. The Bestiary files stay setting-agnostic
    (B9), which is why the Val''loh colour lives here instead.'
